23. g3 {This is my contribution to chess theory. I played the move in some tricky positions to retain control over f4 and give my king some room. Scored 3/3.} Ra5 24. Bf3 Rc8 25. h5 Ra4 26. Rc2 Qf5 $6 27. Qxf5 gxf5 $2 (27... exf5 {is the last chance}) 28. c5 $3 bxc5 29. Rb7 Ra3 (29... Rd8 30. Rxd7 $1) 30. Rxd7 Rxf3 31. h6 Ra3 32. Rxc5 Rf8 33. Rb7 Rd8 ({My opponent was in deep time trouble and failed to find} 33... Rd3 {, the only reasonable move though it does lose prettily:} 34. d7 Rd8 35. Rc8 R3xd7 36. Rbb8 $1 $18) 34. Rcc7 Rd3 35. Rxf7 R3xd6 36. Rxh7 {Source: Conor O'Shaughnessy in 'Dinosaur' (Mitcham CC bulletin, no.21)} 1-0

