1. d4 Nf6 2. Nf3 e6 3. Bf4 c5 4. c3 b6 5. h3 Bb7 6. e3 Be7 7. Nbd2 O-O 8. Be2 d6 9. O-O Nbd7 10. a4 cxd4 11. exd4 Ne4 12. Nxe4 Bxe4 13. Re1 Qc7 14. Bd3 Bxd3 15. Qxd3 Nf6 16. c4 Qb7 17. b3 Rfe8 18. Rec1 a5 19. Rc2 Rad8 20. Be3 g6 21. Rac1 e5 22. Qe2 e4 ({Both sides have been happily ignoring each other, but I felt it was time to gain some space and have a go at him. Perhaps} 22... Nd7 {is more consistent.}) 23. Nd2 Nd7 24. Nb1 f5 25. Nc3 Bf6 26. Nb5 Nb8 27. c5 bxc5 28. dxc5 dxc5 29. Rxc5 Rd3 {I think this position is unclear.} 30. Nc7 $1 Re5 31. R5c4 Qxb3 $5 32. Bd4 Nd7 33. Bxe5 Nxe5 34. Rc5 Rxh3 $2 {Brilliant rubbish, I had about three minutes left, Bronstein ten.} (34... Bg5 35. Re1 Bf4 {with compensation, for example} 36. Rxa5 Rxh3 37. Ra8+ Kf7 38. Ne6 $5 Bh2+ $10) 35. Nd5 Bg5 36. f4 $4 (36. gxh3 Qxh3 (36... Nf3+ $1 37. Kf1 Bxc1 38. Nf6+ Kf7 39. Rxc1 Kxf6 40. Qa6+ Kg5 {with a game still on}) 37. R1c3 Nf3+ 38. Rxf3 exf3 39. Qe8+ Kg7 40. Rc7+ Kh6 41. Qf8+ Kh5 42. Rxh7+) (36. Qb5 $1 Nf3+ (36... Bxc1 37. Qe8+ Kg7 38. Qxe5+ Kh6 39. Rxc1 $18) 37. gxf3 Qxf3 38. Qe8+ Kg7 39. Rc7+ Kh6 40. Qf8+ Kh5 41. Rxh7+ Kg4 42. Rxh3 Kxh3 43. Rc3 $1 $18) 36... Qg3 37. fxg5 (37. fxe5 Qh2+ 38. Kf1 Qh1+ 39. Kf2 Bh4+ 40. g3 Rh2+ 41. Ke3 Rxe2+ 42. Kxe2 Qf3+ 43. Kd2 Qd3+ 44. Ke1 Bxg3#) (37. R5c3 Qh2+ 38. Kf1 Qh1+ 39. Kf2 Bh4+ $19) 37... Nf3+ 38. Qxf3 exf3 39. Rc8+ $4 (39. Nf6+ Kf7 40. Rc7+ Ke6 41. R7c6+ $1 Ke5 42. R6c5+ Kf4 43. R1c4+ Kxg5 $4 44. Ne4+ {, so Black is in perpetual check}) 39... Kf7 40. R1c7+ Ke6 41. Nf4+ Qxf4 42. Rc6+ Kd7 {Source: Conor O'Shaughnessy in 'Dinosaur' (Mitcham CC bulletin, no.21)} 0-1

